WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.980
This is a work of fiction based on research into the period in which it is set. The people,
 organization, laws, and names that appear in it have no relation to any in the real world.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:34.010
Even a holy man
who dwells on the
 borderland between 
life and death,
can never escape
 feeling the sorrow 
of a parting

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.420
I couldn't sleep a wink.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.470
Come on, we're moving out!

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:37.720
Yes, sir.

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:41.590
His Dream

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:43.730
He got away!

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.850
Circle around!

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:47.730
What?!

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:51.480
Vampires, there are two roads open to you!

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.440
One!

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.570
Obey us, Special Forces Unit 16--

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.250
He's... not a vampire.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.170
I see.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:16.680
He wasn't a vampire.
Good thing you didn't kill him.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:17.590
Yes, sir.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.760
But it seems he was an Ascra courier.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:21.680
This?

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.600
He's an underworld transporter.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.480
His job is to carry goods to designated points.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:30.900
He doesn't seem to know anything about Ascra.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:34.780
I've assigned Code Zero
to investigate for the present.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:37.070
Where was it sent to?

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:41.910
It seems we captured him
before he received that order.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:45.540
I suppose you should have
let him go free longer, then.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.460
My apologies, sir.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:51.840
Moriyama, wasn't it? The man
who was killed in action earlier.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.090
Yes, sir.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:56.970
We lost another young man who will be missed.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.640
It's frustrating.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.140
I regret his loss as well.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:06.850
I lost a lot of my men
on the battlefield, you know.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:10.850
I don't want to lose anyone else.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:16.280
That's why we must perfect
our vampire units as soon as possible.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.200
I agree, sir.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.780
I will return to the scene
and search for clues to--

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:24.280
No, I have a request for you.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.080
What, sir?

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:29.790
I have a meeting with the army
top brass tomorrow morning.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.080
I'd like you to accompany me.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.090
Me, sir?

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:36.420
I see.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.420
So, you found a courier.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:42.180
But we've got nothing to go on beyond that.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.100
Have you examined the contents, Mr. Takeuchi?

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.350
Yes. It contained the V Virus.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.980
Hey, that's classified!

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:50.940
Who cares, Yamagami?

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:56.400
We're in a give-and-take,
same-boat relationship with Tenmanya.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:02.490
Your sunscreen ointment was
well received by ladies and sold rather well.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:04.580
Isn't that right, head clerk?

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:08.700
What the hell are you doing on the sly?!

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:13.130
Developing pharmaceuticals <i>is </i>my original job.

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:17.130
It's my work with Code Zero
that's more of a sideline.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:20.720
By the way, Takeuchi,
how did you become a vampire?

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.090
A laboratory accident.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:28.770
The army hired the pharmaceutical company
I worked at to study vampire blood.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.350
And while I was working...

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.520
Talk about bad luck.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.110
My condolences.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:38.940
What are you talking about?

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:42.070
I'm overjoyed about it.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:45.240
I have a brain that will never age.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:49.080
I can pursue the mysteries of our world forever.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:53.790
It's a price I paid to obtain
the wisdom of the world, like Odin.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:58.210
He's a vampire with an interest
in intellectual cravings.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:01.420
That makes him a little
different from the rest of you.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.840
He's certainly different from us.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.140
What about Suwa?

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:08.680
Far be it for me to tell how others feel.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:15.100
Still, Suwa has survived as a vampire
the longest of any of us.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:15.980
How long?

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:19.190
Since before the Edo period, or so I've heard.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:20.730
That long ago?

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.030
How has he...?

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:25.410
That's why middlemen like us are necessary.

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:26.990
What do you mean?

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.870
Head clerk.

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:30.080
What's that?

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:32.750
Registration papers we've prepared.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:38.000
We live in a world where you can find out
who someone is and where they're from.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:42.970
The system of official registration
put vampires in a difficult position.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:46.590
Because if someone reports,
"That guy's a vampire!"

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:51.060
they'd get dragged out into
the sunlight, and that's all she wrote.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:54.100
Vampires are weak, you see.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.020
They live in fear.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:58.980
And the Tenmanya comes to their aid.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.190
Isn't that right, head clerk?

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:07.570
Frailty, thy name is vampire, you might say.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:11.290
Oh, and your families have been
sent notices of your deaths.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:12.490
No one told me!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:18.920
So, try to move in darkness to avoid
bumping into anyone you know.

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:20.960
Like proper vampires.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:32.180
I guess Western things
just don't sit right with me.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.890
There! The Covered Wagon!

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:36.270
Special show... Sold out?!

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:40.230
What should I do? I really
want to go if Raiyu is narrating.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.820
Oh, excuse me!

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:44.070
Who's today's movie narrator?

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.650
Bang.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:51.280
Umm, excuse me?

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.620
Why was that guy wearing a mask? Suspicious...

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.170
I wonder what he was doing here.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.290
Oh, Defrott.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.470
Defrott, where have you been?

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:14.350
You were the one who suddenly ran off, miss.

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:17.890
What is a monster like that doing here?

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.100
That's a bad sign.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:23.110
Sorry, the special showing caught my eye.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:30.240
Come one, come all! Step up and have a look!

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:36.700
I bet Tomiko would be sad if she saw me now.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:39.040
Who's Tomiko?

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.500
My wife.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.750
You were married, Yamagami?

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:45.130
What do you take me for?

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:46.630
I'm sorry.

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:51.680
I wonder what makes us
so different from these people.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.220
Huh?

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:57.220
Chinese lanterns?

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.270
The Day of 46,000 Blessings, huh?

00:08:59.270 --> 00:09:00.140
The what?

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.440
A festival at Sensoji Temple.

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:06.860
Since the Edo period, if there are
festival days on July 9th and 10th,

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:10.320
they say it's worth 46,000 days of blessings.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:14.280
But what does that have to do
with Chinese lantern plants?

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:14.150
Hozuki-Ichi Fair

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:18.950
They say the fruit cures disease
if you swallow it whole with water.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:23.750
That overlapped with the festival,
so the Hozuki-Ichi Fair got started.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:26.550
I always used to come with Tomiko.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:31.550
Wow. That means she might be here right now.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:36.220
She must be getting ready
to release a lantern for Bon.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:39.310
Kind of lonely, isn't it?

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:42.770
I wanted to at least wish her well.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.520
Whoa!

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:51.450
Oh, it's you.

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:52.950
What was that about?!

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:55.660
Why were you in such a hurry?

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:59.910
There was a dangerous one.
I'll tell you the rest at HQ.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.330
A report of a vamp sighting?

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:05.540
Yeah, in front of the Denkikan in district 6.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.290
I met a blond kid.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:08.880
He was with a woman.

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:10.260
A blond boy?

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:12.470
What was his name...?

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:14.970
Are there child vampires?

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:17.510
There are few reported cases.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:21.020
If you mean minors,
Suwa falls into that group, too.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:22.940
Younger than me.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:25.980
And clearly higher ranked.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:28.650
Maybe even higher than the new guy.

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:32.610
Higher than Kurusu means
the highest rank, S class.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.660
That's not a comforting thought.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:37.160
And the girl with him?

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.830
His dinner, maybe?

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:40.910
I don't know any more.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:44.080
Then by now, she must be...

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:48.090
Whoops. Looks like the sun's
about to peak over the horizon.

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:51.380
Let's continue the
investigation after nightfall.

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:52.460
I'm going out.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.590
Now?

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:57.930
Lieutenant General Nakajima ordered
me to attend an army conference.

00:10:57.930 --> 00:11:01.100
You haven't slept, right? Get some rest.

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:02.100
I'm fine.

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:04.770
It's time for all of you to sleep now.

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:07.690
Human hours are about to start.

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:17.740
This human combustion case at Tokyo Station.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:20.620
Society is treating it as a joke,

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:25.330
but that was a vampire escaped
from Tsukishima, wasn't it, Nakajima?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:29.380
You don't sufficiently appreciate
the danger. It's inexcusable.

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:35.920
Vampire units are meant to be the cornerstone
of our army against major powers.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:40.850
At this rate, the navy will get all the glory,
and we'll be an afterthought.

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:43.100
Well, Nakajima?

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:46.390
Have you perfected your "vampire units"?

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:52.360
Nakajima, how many years has it been
since you proposed the vampire unit plan?

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:54.230
Twenty years.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:55.900
And its current status?

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:59.780
Special Forces Unit 16 has 80 members.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:02.330
No, how many vampires?

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:06.580
We have four vampire members
who perform special missions.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:07.710
Four?!

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:11.840
After 20 years, you only
have four vampire units?

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:15.630
Human bodies that can adapt
to vampirism are in short supply.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:22.890
One of the four is a high-ranking A-class
vampire, never before confirmed in Japan.

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:30.020
We can expect four vampires led by him
to more than equal an army platoon.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:33.940
Military strength is measured in materiel!
Don't underestimate modern warfare!

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:35.110
Now, now.

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:41.030
Ltg. Nakajima is a hero who returned
to a battlefield for just one of his men.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:43.280
It's only natural.

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:44.990
Then let me ask:

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:53.750
Can you beat England's rumored vampire forces?

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:54.630
Eventually.

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:56.590
That's not good enough.

00:12:56.590 --> 00:13:00.510
Vampires burn and die in sunlight, don't they?

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:04.390
Why not just surround them
in the night and wait for morning?

00:13:04.390 --> 00:13:05.640
Exactly.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:08.480
"Human hours," huh?

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:08.480
We can't afford to spend
our limited budget on fantasies.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:26.660
Nakajima, to be frank,
criticism of Code Zero is intensifying.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.660
It seems that way.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:34.250
Why not consider using their vampire
abilities for intelligence work?

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:36.840
I hear that that's what England does.

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:38.840
That would defeat the point.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:42.760
When the vampire units I envision are perfected,

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:46.600
our army will be reborn
as the strongest on Earth.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:51.310
Still, they aren't just military men.

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:55.480
They each have backers in all sorts of places.

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:58.070
Act humbly and bide your time.

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:01.400
I'll work something out.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:06.490
Just like I arranged for a vampire from England.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:07.990
Still, bullets...

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.910
What about them?

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:15.880
I bet they've never experienced
bullets whistling past their ears.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.260
Where's Maeda?

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:25.470
He left for his conference
this morning and hasn't come back.

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:28.310
He really does work nonstop.

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:30.770
You're sure he's not a vampire unit?

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:33.730
I think he's pushing himself too hard.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:37.310
Speaking of which, what we
do tonight is up to us again.

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:42.070
A special forces unit needs to discipline!
What's wrong with this place?

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:47.030
Well, they can't hold us to human standards.

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.580
We are dead, after all.

00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:52.540
Don't say that. It's depressing.

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:54.670
Just get used to it already.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:56.880
I'm not like you.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.090
Kurusu and I only just died.

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:01.920
It's our first Bon dead.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.010
Get used to it.

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:06.010
Heartless bastard.

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:07.050
Yamagami!

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.390
What is it?

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:10.260
I had a great idea!

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:11.270
Huh?

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:21.230
Materiel is a more realistic use of funds
than spies who can only work at night.

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.860
Oh, splendid.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:24.450
An excellent idea.

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:30.080
You say it's a great idea,

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:33.750
but will this "in a dream" plan of yours work?

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:37.290
Don't worry. We just need
to use our vampire powers.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:45.970
Huh?

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.680
It's a ghost!

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:52.350
What's wrong?

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:55.140
See?

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:58.440
Don't use vampire powers in view of the public!

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:03.230
But if we move fast like that,
people will just think we're ghosts.

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:05.860
And we are officially dead.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:07.860
That's true.

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:10.030
I wonder if I can pull it off.

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:13.490
Tomiko!

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:15.910
So, she did come to release a lantern!

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:16.830
Yeah.

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:17.920
Let's follow her!

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:19.750
Hey, don't rush!

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:23.460
I hear some nations have
restarted submarine development.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:28.050
But public opinion these days
is all for military reduction.

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:31.300
They have no idea how much
we do in the national interest.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:33.010
The age of materiel is coming.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:39.940
To those who have only made war on paper,
the battlefield is a political stage.

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:42.860
They don't fear bullets
flying on the battlefield.

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:47.490
They fear the shots called "public opinion"
fired by civilians used to peace.

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:52.410
No matter what they said,
I don't think I made the wrong choice.

00:16:52.410 --> 00:16:57.540
I can't save a country if
I can't even save one young man.

00:16:57.540 --> 00:17:01.540
I'm sick of young men being wounded.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.380
For my comrades who were sacrificed,

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:08.420
I must see the vampire unit plan through.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:12.010
Even if it means selling my soul to the devil.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:14.470
Code Zero is the cornerstone.

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:20.190
The new A class, Lieutenant Kurusu,
is our strongest home-grown vampire.

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:23.150
I want you to get him ready for action.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.240
I, Yoshinobu Maeda,

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:34.200
am prepared to humbly devote myself
to completing the vampire unit plan.

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:36.790
I'm counting on you.

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:40.000
Colonel Maeda, we've learned
the package's destination.

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:40.870
Where?

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.290
Yoshiwara.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.580
Ltg. Nakajima.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.290
Go at once.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:46.630
Excuse me, sir.

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:52.550
"It vanishes with each step we take."

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:56.050
"How sad this dream within a dream."

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:00.930
Whoa there.

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:13.950
Tomiko.

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:16.280
Are you ready, Yamagami?

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:18.370
Can we really pull this off?

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:19.910
Leave it to me.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:21.160
Here we go.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:34.430
Dear...

00:18:34.430 --> 00:18:36.010
Tomiko...

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:44.810
Have you come from the afterlife to see me?

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:47.820
Huh? Uh, yeah.

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:49.570
Sorry.

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:55.110
"The joy of seeing you again
in such a way feels to me almost

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:58.240
like I am dreaming a dream
from which I will never wake."

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:04.250
"To be in a world ephemeral
as a dream may feel unpleasant,

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:08.590
but we are free to dream
or talk of dreams as we please."

00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:17.260
Who's there?

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.260
Code Zero's Lieutenant Suwa.

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:20.310
Where's Kurusu?

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:22.220
I'm told he's on patrol.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:28.270
Once I get out, go to base and establish
a type-I alert around the scene.

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:29.270
Yes, sir.

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:32.030
Colonel?

00:19:32.030 --> 00:19:34.400
Sorry. My hand slipped.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:41.830
What happened to my harpsichord?

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:44.080
I clean it every day.

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:46.580
And my rosewood armchair?

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:50.380
It's a great help when I'm knitting.

00:19:50.380 --> 00:19:52.710
I see.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:58.390
If you ever have money trouble,
sell all that stuff to support yourself, okay?

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:02.680
Your future is more important
than memories of me.

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:07.480
Things aren't that bad.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:10.730
If you want to...

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:13.940
If you want, you should even remarry.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:17.320
I was hopeless as a husband.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:21.950
But there was never a day
I didn't wish for your happiness.

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:22.700
So--

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:25.660
"Black kites and sparrows,
herons, and even the crows;

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:31.210
What wonder is it if two birds of a like
kind should choose to flock together?"

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:35.960
Tomiko.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:41.260
I'll always be your Tomiko.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:45.720
Please come visit me again,
until I go to join you.

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:54.820
I will.

00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:56.490
I promise.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.920
Were you able to say goodbye?

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:14.460
I'll be asking you again next year.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:16.420
I'll be glad to help.

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:22.220
"The person for whom I had
waited anxiously had finally come;

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:26.680
What can there be to regret
in a meeting such as this?"

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:43.990
See you next year.

00:23:24.550 --> 00:23:28.010
There were no signs of whoever
ate her when I found her.

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:30.140
But if they're still around...

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:38.940
In there, then.

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:47.030
Unknown Song
